[Id "london"]
[Name "London System"]
[Side "white"]
[ECO "D02, A46"]
[Description "1.d4 and 2.Bf4, then the same e3, c3, Nbd2 and Bd3 set-up against almost anything."]
[Tags "system, solid, beginner-friendly"]

1. d4 d5
  (1... Nf6 2. Bf4 g6 {@variation vs King's Indian set-up} 3. e3 {e3 supports d4 and frees the f1 bishop.} 3... Bg7 4. Nf3 O-O 5. Be2 {Be2 is the usual square here: against …g6 the bishop has little to aim at on d3.} 5... d6 6. h3 {h3 gives the f4 bishop a retreat on h2, so …Nh5 can't trade it. [%cal Yf4h2]} (6. O-O {@alt})
{@line id=london-vs-kid level=1 tier=main name="vs King's Indian set-up" summary="Against …g6, keep the pyramid, put the bishop on e2 and play h3 to save the f4 bishop."}
6... Nbd7 7. O-O {O-O: if Black plays …e5, the f4 bishop drops back to h2 and keeps its diagonal.}
{@line id=london-vs-kid-deep level=2 tier=main name="vs King's Indian: 6…Nbd7" summary="Against …Nbd7 and …e5 ideas, just castle; the h2 square keeps your bishop safe."}
)
2. Bf4 {Bf4 develops the bishop before e3 shuts it in.} {@variation Main Line} 2... Nf6
  (2... e6 3. e3 Nf6 4. Nf3 {Nf3: the same position as 2…Nf6 3.e3 e6 4.Nf3.}
{@line id=london-2e6 level=1 tier=main name="vs 2…e6" summary="2…e6 changes nothing: e3, Nf3, and the usual pyramid."}
)
  (2... Nc6 3. e3 Nf6 4. Nf3 {Nf3: develop as usual; c3 and Bd3 come next.}
{@line id=london-2nc6 level=2 tier=main name="vs 2…Nc6" summary="Against 2…Nc6, keep the same set-up: e3, Nf3, then c3 and Bd3."}
)
  (2... c5 3. e3 {e3 backs up d4 and keeps the set-up.} 3... Nc6 4. c3 {c3 holds d4 firmly.} 4... Nf6 5. Nf3 e6 6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. Bg3 O-O 8. Bd3 {Bd3: the same position as the main line.}
{@line id=london-2c5 level=2 tier=side name="vs 2…c5" summary="2…c5 changes nothing: build the same pyramid and you reach the main line."}
)
3. e3 e6
  (3... Bf5 {@variation vs …Bf5} 4. Bd3 {Bd3 offers to trade off Black's best minor piece. [%cal Gd3f5]}
{@line id=london-bf5 level=1 tier=main name="vs 3…Bf5" summary="When Black copies with …Bf5, challenge the bishop with Bd3."}
4... Bxd3 5. Qxd3 e6 6. Nf3 {Nf3: the queen on d3 eyes h7 and supports a later e4. [%cal Ge3e4]}
{@line id=london-bf5-deep level=2 tier=main name="3…Bf5 4.Bd3 Bxd3" summary="After the bishop trade, develop with Nf3 and Nbd2 and prepare e4 with the queen on d3."}
)
  (3... c5 4. c3 {c3 holds d4.} 4... Nc6 5. Nf3 5... e6
    (5... Qb6 {…Qb6 attacks b2, which the f4 bishop no longer defends. [%cal Rb6b2]} 6. Qb3 {Qb3 offers a queen trade that would open the a-file for White's rook.} (6. Qc2 {@alt}) 6... c4 7. Qc2 {Qc2 keeps the queen; White wants e4 next to break the black centre. [%cal Ge3e4]}
{@line id=london-qb6 level=2 tier=side name="vs …c5 and …Qb6" summary="Meet …Qb6 with Qb3 (or Qc2); if …c4 kicks the queen, go to c2 and aim for e4."}
)
  6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. Bg3 O-O 8. Bd3 {Bd3: the same position as the main line.}
{@line id=london-3c5 level=1 tier=side name="vs 3…c5" summary="Different move order, same London: keep building the pyramid."}
)
4. Nf3 c5
  (4... Bd6 5. Bg3 {Bg3 keeps the bishop; if Black takes, hxg3 opens the h-file.} 5... O-O 6. Bd3 {Bd3 aims at h7, as in the main line. [%cal Yd3h7]}
{@line id=london-bd6 level=1 tier=main name="vs 4…Bd6" summary="Against …Bd6, retreat to g3 instead of trading, then Bd3 and the usual pyramid."}
6... c5 7. c3 Nc6 8. Nbd2 {Nbd2: the same position as the main line.}
{@line id=london-bd6-deep level=2 tier=main name="4…Bd6 into the main line" summary="…Bd6 and …c5 bring us to the main line: Bg3, Bd3, c3, Nbd2."}
)
5. c3 {c3 holds the d4 pawn firmly against …c5.} 5... Nc6 6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. Bg3 {Bg3 keeps the bishop when …Bd6 offers a trade, and opens the h-file if Black takes.} 7... O-O 8. Bd3 {Bd3 aims at Black's king; Ne5 and a kingside attack can follow. [%cal Gf3e5]}
{@line id=london-main level=1 tier=side name="Main Line vs …d5, …c5" summary="Bf4, e3, Nf3, c3, Nbd2, Bd3: the London pyramid, the same set-up every time."}
8... b6 9. Ne5 {Ne5 grabs the outpost and starts a kingside attack.} 9... Bb7 10. f4 {f4 supports the e5 knight, a Stonewall-style attacking set-up.}
{@line id=london-main-deep level=2 tier=side name="Ne5 and f4" summary="When Black plays slowly, put a knight on e5, back it with f4 and attack the king."} *
